<title>FRANCE: France keeps Thomson-CSF timetable.</title>
<headline>France keeps Thomson-CSF timetable.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The timetable for the sale by the government of a 58-percent stake in defence electronics firm Thomson-CSF is unchanged, a spokeswoman for the Finance Ministry said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>She was speaking after the sale of shares in France Telecom SA was delayed by a month in order not to clash with a snap parliamentary election called by President Jacques Chirac on Monday evening.</p>
<p>The final bids for Thomson-CSF have to be submitted before May 7. Alcatel Alsthom is making a joint bid with Dassault Industrie and Lagardere Groupe is also making a bid.</p>
<p>Britain's GEC Plc, which was not allowed to make a separate bid, is in talks with the bidders to see whether it can join.</p>
